### Categories: run top to bottom with the VS Code "REST Client" extension
### (or any .http runner). Seed data gives categories 1-3: `python -m app.seed`
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

### List categories (sorted by name, paginated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories?skip=0&limit=50

### Get one category
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories/1

### Create a category  -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Knitwear",
  "description": "Cardigans, jumpers and scarves"
}

### Duplicate name (case-insensitive)  -> 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "knitwear" }

### Replace a category (PUT)  -> 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/categories/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Dresses",
  "description": "Summer and evening dresses"
}

### Missing category  -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories/99999

### Validation error (empty name)  -> 422
POST {{baseUrl}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "" }

### Delete a category that still has products  -> 409 (an empty category gives 204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/categories/1
